  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula for ferrous ammonium sulphate is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. It is prepared by dissolving equimolar mixture of hydrated ferrous sulphate and ammonium sulphate&nbsp;in water containing a little sulphuric acid. The solution is subjected to crystallisation, ferrous ammonium sulphate separates out from the solution.</p><p>The chemical reaction is given below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>Mohr</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>salt</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Avoid prolonged heating while preparing crystals of ferrous ammonium sulphate, as it may oxidise ferrous ions to ferric ions and change the stoichiometry of the crystals.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
